WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.120
"Like Beet Juice, Taurine Supplementation
May Only Be Safe in the Context of a Plant-Based Diet"

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:09.760
In my last videos,
I mentioned how the best choice

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.000
might be to eat
a healthy plant-based diet

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.320
with supplemental taurine,

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.560
but it’s possible
that taking taurine,

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.960
whether from bulk powder,
supplements, energy drinks,

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.160
or even shellfish,

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.960
may only be safe in the context
of a healthy plant-based diet.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.760
In the remarkable study that
launched this video series,

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.760
taurine supplementation
of lab animals

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.640
increased their lifespan
and/or healthspan.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.120
However, the impact of taurine
dietary supplementation

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.040
on the gut microbiome
was not addressed.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.200
Oral administration of taurine

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.560
results in an increase

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.760
of taurine-conjugated
bile acids,

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.600
for example,
quadrupling the percentage

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.920
of taurocholic acid.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.440
That’s not good,

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.920
because higher levels
of taurocholic acid in humans

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.040
is associated
with a shorter lifespan.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.560
For each
standard deviation increase

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.160
in a measure
of taurocholate,

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.240
which is just buffered
taurocholic acid,

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.880
the odds of achieving
longevity in humans

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.518
appeared to decrease
by almost 40 percent,

00:01:07.518 --> 00:01:11.040
a 30 percent lower chance
of making it to age 80.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:14.000
What happens is the metabolism

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.640
of these
taurine-conjugated bile acids

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.800
by our gut microbes
generates the rotten egg gas,

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.880
hydrogen sulfide,

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.120
which doesn’t
just give you smelly farts,

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.080
but is a DNA-damaging compound.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.000
So, hydrogen sulfide could be

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.160
a significant
bacterial metabolite

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.320
that initiates colon cancer.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:35.760
And that’s just the half of it.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:39.040
Taurocholic acid gets split
into taurine and cholic acid.

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.680
The taurine goes on
to produce hydrogen sulfide,

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:44.640
which is pro-inflammatory
and could trigger DNA mutations,

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.960
and the cholic acid
gets turned into a toxic,

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.560
so-called secondary bile acid,
called deoxycholic acid,

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:54.080
known as DCA, which also
produces inflammation

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.720
and can promote growing tumors.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.600
So, gut microbes can
metabolize the taurocholic acid

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:01.920
into hydrogen sulfide and DCA,

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.720
which are genotoxins
and tumor promoters,

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.200
respectively,
and could intensify

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.440
aging symptoms in the host.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.880
Therefore, consumption
of a diet low in taurine

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:16.560
may contribute to the reduced
frequency of cancer.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.080
Taurine can promote the growth

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.400
of a taurine-metabolizing
bacteria,

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.560
Bilophila wadsworthia,
which thrive on taurine.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.040
Those bacteria take the taurine

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.920
and turn it
into hydrogen sulfide,

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.640
which is linked to a weaker
colonic mucus barrier,

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.200
inflammatory bowel disease,
and colorectal cancer.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.560
So, it’s not just cancer.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:35.760
The increased taurocholate

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.520
caused by
taurine supplementation

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.160
is associated with
a reduced lifespan in humans

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.240
in the absence
of any relation to risk

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.600
for cardiovascular disease
or for cancer.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.920
But the effects
of hydrogen sulfide

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:50.080
can be stopped.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.960
The cells that line our colon
express protective enzymes

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:55.760
that can detoxify
hydrogen sulfide.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.920
How can we boost those enzymes?

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.880
Butyrate boosts those
detoxification enzymes,

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:04.080
protecting our cells
from the sulfide gas.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.280
Remember butyrate?

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.560
That’s what our good
gut bugs make from fiber.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.760
So, there’s this struggle
between the sulfide

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.600
made by the bad bugs in the gut

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:17.040
versus the butyrate made
by the good bugs in our gut.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.600
Hydrogen sulfide can cause
hyperproliferation,

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:22.080
a signal of potential
colon cancer development,

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:25.280
but it can be reversed
if you drip on some butyrate,

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:26.560
like you would get naturally

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.120
by just eating
a high-fiber diet.

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.440
That’s just half
of the protection, though.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.600
The sulfur-containing
amino acids, like taurine,

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.440
and diets high in animal protein

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.560
aren’t the only factors
that select for the bad bacteria

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:40.720
that create the toxic,
tumor-promoting,

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.400
secondary bile acids,

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.040
there’s also the animal fat.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:46.880
When people were given taurine,

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:48.880
like the half a gram
three times a day

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:50.720
I suggested in my last video,

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.000
there was a marked increase

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.760
in the proportion of
taurine-conjugated bile acids,

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:56.800
but what we care about

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:00.960
is how many are actually
excreted into our gut.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:02.640
This is how it’s envisioned.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.240
On an animal-based diet,
not only is there more taurine,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:09.520
leading to a higher ratio of
taurine-conjugated bile acids,

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.600
but also more bile secretion

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.080
owing to
the higher fat consumption.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.360
High-fat diets are associated

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:18.960
with increased taurine
conjugation in humans,

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:22.800
but not just any fat,
specifically saturated fat.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.720
Consumption of a diet
high in saturated fat,

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.640
in this case butter fat,
but not vegetable oil fat,

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:31.040
promotes the expansion
of the hydrogen-sulfide

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:32.800
generating bad bacteria,

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.840
and effects are mediated
by milk-fat promoted

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.080
taurine-conjugation bile acids.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:40.640
So, to counter
any negative effects

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:42.720
of excess taurine consumption,

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.360
we should eat a high-fiber diet

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:47.520
low in saturated fat,
in other words,

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:51.200
a diet centered
around whole plant foods.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:54.480
It reminds me of the whole,
"Vegetable nitrate strategy,"

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.080
to boost athletic performance

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.920
and slow muscle
and artery aging,

00:04:57.920 --> 00:04:59.280
or slow aging, period,

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.920
by reducing
our resting metabolic rate.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.560
As I discuss in my book,
How Not to Age,

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:07.760
the nitrate strategy
may only be safe

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.640
in the context
of a plant-based diet.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:12.880
If you feed people
an amine-rich diet,

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:14.320
in other words
a single meal a day

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:16.640
with cod, salmon,
shrimp, or pollack,

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.320
along with
the nitrate equivalent

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:20.080
of half a cup (120 ml)
of beet juice,

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.520
you get a big jump
in the amount

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:26.320
of carcinogenic nitrosamines
flowing through your system.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:28.240
You get a similar reaction

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:30.160
combining the same amount
of beet juice equivalents

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.280
with poultry, chicken,
or turkey breasts.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.920
The nitrates turn into nitrites,

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.080
which mix
with the amines and amides

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.600
concentrated in animal foods

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:43.040
to form carcinogenic
nitrosamines and nitrosamides,

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:45.440
doubling levels within a week.

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:48.080
This explains
why having omnivores

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.000
drink a single bottle
of beet juice

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.280
can lead
to a significant rise

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.440
in these
carcinogenic compounds

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:56.400
flowing through their system
within 24 hours.

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.000
But what are the inhibitors

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.480
of this reaction
for cancer prevention?

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:01.920
Vitamin C, polyphenols,

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.800
and other antioxidants
found in plant foods.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.200
So, we can add some vitamin C
to that beet juice,

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.280
and there’s less of a problem.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:11.040
Just like
a healthy plant-based diet

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:13.680
may be necessary
to take safe advantage

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.520
of nitrate supplementation,

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.080
a healthy plant-based diet
may also be necessary

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:20.720
to take safe advantage
of any potential benefits

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:24.016
of taurine supplementation.

